== a_fill_of_another_type
error[Z0214]: `coalesce` needs values of one type, but these are an Int and a Str (row 1)
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:17
  |
2 | d.plot(x: x, y: fill_missing(k, "a")).points()
  |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ values of two types
  |
  = help: Int and Float join as Float, and NA fits any type; convert with `to` where a mixture is meant

== an_argument_left_out
error[Z0406]: `clamp` needs `high`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:17
  |
2 | d.plot(x: x, y: clamp(x, 0)).points()
  |                 ^^^^^ `high` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `clamp(x, low, high)`

== a_function_that_gives_no_value
error[Z0401]: an expression mapped to an aesthetic cannot use `assert`, which gives no value
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:17
  |
2 | d.plot(x: x, y: assert(x > 0, "positive")).points()
  |                 ^^^^^^ not kept in a mapping
  |
  = help: a mapping is computed from variables, numbers, the operators and the functions of `core`, `time` and `text`, as in `log(wage)`, `wage / hours` or `year(hired)`; compute anything else with `add` first and map the new variable

